{"type":"exercise","type_name":"Exercise","number":"","title":"C1","title_html":"C1","html":"<p>In <span class=\"citation\" data-cites=\"exm-add-gam\">@exm-add-gam</span> the curve above a disease\nindex of <span class=\"math inline\"><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"CHTML\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\" data-tex=\"40\"><mjx-math class=\" MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c34\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c30\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>40</mn></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></span> rests on <span class=\"math inline\"><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"CHTML\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\" data-tex=\"55\"><mjx-math class=\" MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c35\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c35\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>55</mn></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></span> observations. Suppose all of them were\ndeleted. Using the fact that the P-spline penalty of <span class=\"citation\" data-cites=\"def-smo-pspline\">@def-smo-pspline</span>\nhas the straight lines as its null space, describe exactly what the\nfitted curve does over the empty range, and compute the limit of its\nvariance as the range of emptiness grows.</p>","file":"ch44-additive-models/06-generalized-additive-models.html"}